WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:07.880
The average American will move 11.3 times
over the course of their life.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.220
There are many different reasons: finding
a better home, finding a cheaper home, getting

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.710
a new job, getting married, going to college,
getting evicted…

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:20.619
Whether it’s a happy reason or a bummer,
I don’t know anyone who actually enjoys

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.210
the process of moving.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.429
The planning, the packing, the cleaning, the
expense.

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:27.099
But we’ve got your back!

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:29.669
No, we can’t actually help you load the
truck.

00:00:29.669 --> 00:00:30.669
Sorry.

00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:33.760
But we do have 9 hacks to save money on your
move.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.160
You may have to break your back, but you can
avoid breaking the bank.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.600
Look around your house.

00:00:50.609 --> 00:00:54.710
How many individual “things” do you think
are in it?

00:00:54.710 --> 00:01:00.550
If it’s the average American household,
that number is 300,000.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:05.560
The idea of transporting 300,000 items from
one location to another is… daunting.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.510
And the more you have to move, the more expensive
it will be.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:13.159
So let’s get that number down, shall we?

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:16.880
When you’re a month or two out, make a list
of all the rooms in your house and focus on

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.580
one per week.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:22.500
Your job is to pick up every item in that
room and ask yourself if you really still

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.500
like it.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.320
This is not the time to be precious!

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.060
Aunt Helga will never find out you got rid
of her lamp.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.140
You can sell the unwanted items online, or
just donate them to a local charity.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:38.070
As long as it’s not broken or filthy, Goodwill
will take just about anything!

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:44.420
For a lot of different reasons, summer is
the most popular time to move.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.420
More than 30 million Americans move at this
time of year, and another 30 million are traveling

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.710
for vacation, which means the highways are
packed, and so are movers’ schedules.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.820
If you can wait until the fall or early winter,
it can save you money.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:03.180
Movers are less busy so they will sometimes
lower their rates by up to 30%.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.600
And less traffic on the roads means more efficient
travel times.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.190
And if you’re loading the truck yourself,
wouldn’t you rather do it when it’s not

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.610
100 degrees?

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:18.270
If you’re a renter, there are a variety
of reasons that a landlord can refuse to give

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:23.250
your security deposit back, so reread your
lease terms to make sure you’re in compliance.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:28.800
Getting a check for a couple thousand can
be a huge help in offsetting your moving costs.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:37.880
You can hire movers to do EVERYTHING--pack,
load, drive, unload, unpack--but it gets expensive!

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:43.760
An inter-city move of a two bedroom apartment
would cost us about two grand here in Austin.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.700
Maybe that’s why only 21% of people use
professionals from start to finish.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:53.340
Instead, if you pack your own things, rent
your own van and drive it yourself, suddenly

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:58.450
you’re only paying $500 for the load-in
and load-out, which, let’s be honest, is

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.160
no one’s favorite part of the job.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:08.420
1 out of 10 moves are for work, and if that
includes you, you should definitely inquire

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.230
about a relo package as part of your contract.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.310
39% of all moving shipments are actually paid
for by corporations.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:19.590
And unlike salary, it’s a one-time expense
that often comes from a different part of

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.430
the company’s budget, so they might be more
open to it than you think.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.700
Remember, if you don’t ask, the answer is
always NO.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:36.020
Why spend money on packing material when you
have already have closets of soft stuff at

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.020
hand?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.290
Wrap your dishes and other breakables in clothes,
towels and linens to protect them and cut

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.290
down on waste.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:46.280
Sure, it’s a little heavier than styrofoam
or bubble wrap, but you’re bringing this

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.380
stuff along anway!

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.160
As my Uncle Olav used to say, “Only a sucker
pays for cardboard boxes.”

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.950
Okay, I don’t have an Uncle Olav, but seriously,
there are SO many places to get them for free:

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.790
Craigslist, Facebook, NextDoor, Freecycle,
or drop by your local grocery or liquor stores--they

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.150
may be happy to let you take them off their
hands.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:17.900
And, yes, I have personally pulled boxes out
of recycling dumpsters behind a hardware store.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:26.360
It’s actually pretty common for people to
leave the fridge and pantry till the last

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.960
minute, and then decide they’d rather throw
everything away than worry about perishables

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.260
going bad in a hot moving truck.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:36.599
This is such a waste of food, especially considering
it can cost hundreds to restock a pantry from

00:04:36.599 --> 00:04:37.900
scratch in your new home.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.099
So in the weeks before your move, commit to
consuming as much as you can from what you

00:04:42.099 --> 00:04:43.240
already have.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.680
The things you can’t eat will probably fit
into one or two plastic tubs you can transport

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.680
yourself.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.070
Honestly, a bottle of olive oil can cost 10
bucks.

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.340
That baby is coming with me!

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.360
This is probably the most important money-saving
tip we can give you.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.690
Wanna sell your furniture instead of giving
it away?

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.060
That takes time.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.120
Wanna find free boxes instead of buying them?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.389
That takes time.

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:16.639
Wanna properly clean your apartment so you
can get your security deposit back?

00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:18.639
That takes time.

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:23.120
Moving always takes longer than you think,
and the more rushed you are, the more it’ll

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.120
cost you.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.509
So kick off your moving plan at least two
months in advance of your last day in your

00:05:28.509 --> 00:05:29.509
old home.

00:05:29.509 --> 00:05:32.599
It will also make the experience safer and
more pleasant.

00:05:32.599 --> 00:05:38.729
Oh, and chiropractors are expensive, so lift
with your legs, not with your back.

00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:39.800
And that’s our two cents!

